{"name":"Patient White","hex":"#ede2de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"patient","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Willing to wait if necessary; not losing one's temper while waiting.","Constant in pursuit or exertion; persevering; calmly diligent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or animal that receives health care from a doctor, nurse, dentist, allied health practitioner, or other person educated in health care.","The noun or noun phrase that is semantically on the receiving end of a verb's action."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patient"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Patient","blocks":[{"text":"A patient is any recipient of health care services that are performed by healthcare professionals. The patient is most often ill or injured and in need of treatment by a physician, nurse, optometrist, dentist, veterinarian, or other health care provider."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patient","wikidata":"Q181600"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb